    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Psychedelic preparation &amp; integration</p>
      <h2 id="psychedelic-title">A psychedelic experience.<br /><em>And life after it.</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">An experience can leave you with insight, uncertainty, or more than you know what to do with. There is room to explore all of it here.</p>
      <p>I offer preparation, screening conversations, intention-setting, and harm-reduction support. After an experience, integration gives us time to explore what happened, what it means to you, and how it connects to your everyday life.</p>
      <p>You don&rsquo;t need a clear story or a positive experience to begin. Integration can be part of ongoing therapy, with space to return to what emerges over time.</p>
      <aside class="scope-note"><strong>A note about scope</strong><p>I don&rsquo;t provide recommendations to pursue psychedelic medicines or referrals to underground providers. My role is therapeutic support through preparation, harm reduction, and integration.</p></aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
